<https://id.dalia.education/learning-resource/d4b9f978-8302-408f-b215-fe717ce904fa> a ec:EducationalResource ;
    dcterms:description "The Digital Humanities Virtual Laboratory Lab (\"DHVLab\", Digital Teaching and Research Infrastructure for the Humanities) at Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München has developed a modular teaching and research infrastructure within the project framework and for students of art, history and linguistics who are particularly concerned with methods of the Digital Humanities. In the process, manuals as well as detailed descriptions of user cases have also been produced, including an introduction to dealing with databases. The manuals offer an insight into information technology fields that have been developed with practical relevance and the demands of students in the humanities in mind." ;
